I've already read RIGGING.md, the feature file, the step definitions, the checker, and the production seam (js/app.js). Per crew's "second pass, one retrieval", I have everything. I already inspected the failure: it's the re-entrancy guard in commitEdit/handleEditBlur.

Now the fix. The scantling's invariant: "Committing an edit ends the editing session before the post-commit render(), so a re-entrant blur handler is a no-op rather than re-invoking the commit and double-removing the node."

Acceptance check A: commitEdit removes the 'editing' class from the committed list item before it calls render().

So the smallest change: in commitEdit, before each `render()` call, add `li.classList.remove('editing')`. Let me look at the current commitEdit code again:

```js
  function commitEdit(li, raw) {
    var title = li.querySelector('label').textContent;
    var value = raw.trim();
    var todos = load();
    if (value === '') {
      var remaining = todos.filter(function (t) { return t.title !== title; });
      save(remaining);
      render();
      return;
    }
    for (var i = 0; i < todos.length; i++) {
      if (todos[i].title === title) {
        todos[i].title = value;
        break;
      }
    }
    save(todos);
    render();
